AIM: To implement Network Address Translation (NAT) to translate private IP addresses into public IP addresses.


Topology
Devices: - 2 Routers PT: R0 and R1- 2 Switches PT- 2 PCs: PC0 and PC1 - 1 Server: Server0
Connections: - PC0 and Server0 connect to Switch0.- Switch0 connects to R0.- R0 connects to R1 using Serial2/0.
- R1 connects to Switch1.- Switch1 connects to PC1.
Use automatic connection in Packet Tracer, as specified in your journal.

Configure Host IPs and Gateways:
Set PC0 to IP 10.10.10.2, mask 255.255.255.0, default gateway 10.10.10.1.
Set Server0 to IP 10.10.10.3, mask 255.255.255.0, default gateway 10.10.10.1.
Set PC1 to IP 20.20.20.2, mask 255.255.255.0, default gateway 20.20.20.1.



ROUTER0 CONFIGURATION(Interfaces and Static Routes):
enable
configure terminal
interface FastEthernet0/0
ip address 10.10.10.1 255.255.255.0
ip nat inside
no shutdown
exit
interface Serial2/0
ip address 192.162.10.1 255.255.255.0
ip nat outside
no shutdown
exit
ip route 60.0.0.0 255.0.0.0 192.162.10.2

Configure Static NAT Mappings on Router0:
ip nat inside source static 10.10.10.2 50.50.50.2
ip nat inside source static 10.10.10.3 50.50.50.3
end

ROUTER1 CONFIGURATION(Interfaces and Static Routes):
enable
configure terminal
interface FastEthernet0/0
 ip address 20.20.20.1 255.255.255.0
 ip nat inside
 no shutdown
 exit
interface Serial2/0
 ip address 192.162.10.2 255.255.255.0
 ip nat outside
 no shutdown
 exit
ip route 50.0.0.0 255.0.0.0 192.162.10.1
ip nat inside source static 20.20.20.2 60.60.60.2
end


PING EXTERNAL AND INTERNAL IPS AND CHECK
PC0 - ping 60.60.60.2 and 20.20.20.2
PC1 - ping 50.50.50.2 and 10.10.10.2
